Representations. The Seller represents and warrants that:
(a) it has full legal and beneficial title to the Shares, free from all encumbrances;
(b) the Seller is duly incorporated and has the requisite power and authority to enter into this Agreement;
(c) the financial statements are accurate and prepared in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles;
(d) to the Seller’s knowledge, the Target is in compliance with applicable laws;
(e) there are no undisclosed material liabilities as of the date hereof;
(f) to the Seller’s knowledge, there is no material litigation pending or threatened against the Target; and
(g) there has been no material adverse change in the Target’s business since the date of the last financial statements provided to the Buyer.
Each of the foregoing representations and warranties is subject to disclosures in the Disclosure Schedule and shall survive Closing for a period of two (2) years, except as otherwise required by law.

6. Closing Deliverables. At closing, Seller shall deliver:
(a) duly executed share transfer documents;
(b) updated register of members;
(c) copies of board resolutions approving the transfer;
(d) resignation letters of the Seller’s nominated directors and officers, if required by Buyer.
Buyer to deliver Purchase Price and any required deliverables as reasonably agreed.

3. Representations. The Seller represents and warrants to the Buyer that:
(a) the Seller is the sole legal and beneficial owner of, and has good and marketable title to, the Shares, free and clear of all liens and encumbrances;
(b) the financial statements provided to the Buyer are accurate and complete in all material respects as of the date of this Agreement;
(c) to the Seller's knowledge, the Seller has no undisclosed liabilities, other than those disclosed in the financial statements or incurred in the ordinary course of business since the balance sheet date;
(d) the Seller is in compliance in all material respects with applicable laws in relation to the Shares and the business;
(e) there is no pending or, to the Seller's knowledge, threatened litigation or governmental proceeding against the Seller relating to the Shares;
(f) the Seller has duly and timely paid all material taxes related to the Shares and the business, or has adequate reserves set aside for the payment thereof;
(g) since the balance sheet date, there has not been any material adverse change in the business, operations, or financial condition of the company, other than as disclosed to the Buyer in writing.

3. Representations. The Seller represents and warrants that:
  (a) it has authority to enter into this Agreement and perform its obligations;
  (b) it holds good and marketable title to the Shares, free of liens and encumbrances;
  (c) the most recent financial statements provided to the Buyer are accurate in all material respects;
  (d) there are no undisclosed material liabilities relating to the Seller or the Shares;
  (e) it is in compliance with all applicable laws in all material respects;
  (f) it is not party to any material contract not disclosed to the Buyer, and,
  (g) it has not received written notice of any litigation or governmental proceeding pending or threatened against the Seller or the Shares.

[ins] The Seller further warrants, as of the date hereof and as of Closing:
(a) there are no material undisclosed liabilities;
(b) all applicable laws have been complied with;
(c) the operation of the business has not breached any material contracts or laws to the Seller's knowledge.
These warranties are subject to disclosures and limitations customary for transactions of this nature, to be further discussed.[/ins]
